Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='publictree', at=datetime(2026, 10, 4, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='One matcher guards the public tree: public-tree.sh writes it and the leak guard refuses any line naming this deployment', body="The one matcher is `scripts/public-tree.sh --check`: `public-tree.sh <out>` writes the tree a public repository would start from (every committed file but the private history `.gitattributes` declares `export-ignore`, the reports, the CLAUDE history and the changelog, which starts afresh from `scripts/public-changelog.md`), and `public_tree_holds_nothing_of_this_deployment` fails on any line of it holding an address outside the reserved domains, a `.ts.net` name, a home path, this deployment's box, tailnet or user (read from `<data>/FETCHER`, the instance's `app_url` and its roots), or a term of the two private lists (`context-terms.txt` beside the first), or a relative link of a front page (`README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `SECURITY.md`, `docs/README.md`) naming no file of the tree. Box facts live in the data repository: `<data>/FETCHER`, `<data>/VAULT_RECIPIENT`, and the Android portal's box and sender, which the release workflow writes into the APK's profile from the repository's `SUZATARY_PORTAL_*`. The matcher is pinned separately, against a throwaway tree and deployment. Since 2026-10-09 it is the binary's (`suzatary_core::leak`, `suzatary leaks`), which also refuses a tailnet node's address and a telephone number.", rationale="The one matcher since 2026-10-04; the binary's since 2026-10-09.", supersedes=()))